{"license":"CC-BY-4.0","fileAccessRequest":true,"metadataBlocks":{"citation":{"displayName":"Citation Metadata","name":"citation","fields":[{"typeName":"title","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"COVID-19 and (ir)responsible mobility:  Reading counter-practices through Derrida"},{"typeName":"alternativeTitle","multiple":true,"typeClass":"primitive","value":["Interviews in Paris Nov and Dec. 2022"]},{"typeName":"otherId","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"otherIdAgency":{"typeName":"otherIdAgency","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"DANS-KNAW"},"otherIdValue":{"typeName":"otherIdValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"easy-dataset:321418"}}]},{"typeName":"author","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"authorName":{"typeName":"authorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"R Puggioni"},"authorAffiliation":{"typeName":"authorAffiliation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"LUISS University"},"authorIdentifierScheme":{"typeName":"authorIdentifierScheme","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"ORCID"},"authorIdentifier":{"typeName":"authorIdentifier","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"0000-0002-0668-6299"}}]},{"typeName":"datasetContact","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"datasetContactName":{"typeName":"datasetContactName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Raffaela  rpuggioni"}}]},{"typeName":"dsDescription","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"dsDescriptionValue":{"typeName":"dsDescriptionValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"<p>During the COVID-19 pandemic, issues of (civic) (ir)responsibility were raised virtually every time people broke immobility rules. I have investigated the relationship between mobility and (ir)responsibility by focussing on the creative modalities through which (some) people in Paris circumvented mobility restrictions. Here I provide the transcripts of the interviews carried out between November and December 2022.<br>These interviews have been conducted as part of the following: MOBILISE project - Marie Skłodowska-Curie grant agreement no. 101024492: ‘MOBILISE: Stay home: Emergency, (im)mobility, and the liberal subject’, and included in the following article: COVID-19 and (ir)responsible mobility:  Reading counter-practices through Derrida, submitted in Open Research Europe, in the collection ‘The Future of Democracy’.<\/p>"}},{"dsDescriptionValue":{"typeName":"dsDescriptionValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"<p>Interviews in Paris Nov and Dec. 2022<\/p>"}},{"dsDescriptionValue":{"typeName":"dsDescriptionValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Date Submitted: 2023-09-26"}}]},{"typeName":"subject","multiple":true,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":["Social Sciences"]},{"typeName":"keyword","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Political ethics"}}]},{"typeName":"language","multiple":true,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":["English","French"]},{"typeName":"productionDate","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"2023-05-31"},{"typeName":"distributionDate","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"2023-09-26"},{"typeName":"dateOfDeposit","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"2023-09-26"}]},"dansRights":{"displayName":"Rights Metadata","name":"dansRights","fields":[{"typeName":"dansRightsHolder","multiple":true,"typeClass":"primitive","value":["Marie-Curie Fellow R Puggioni (LUISS University)","Marie-Curie Fellow R Puggioni (LUISS University)"]},{"typeName":"dansPersonalDataPresent","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"Unknown"},{"typeName":"dansMetadataLanguage","multiple":true,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":["English"]}]},"dansRelationMetadata":{"displayName":"Relation Metadata","name":"dansRe